WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.400
Most people don't know how to market

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:04.120
outside of like, "Oh, just put up a

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:05.760
Facebook ad and hope that you get

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:07.160
something." Or in the real estate world,

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:08.640
they don't know how to market outside of

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:10.000
put an ad on Zillow and hope you get

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:13.360
something on on Craigslist or on

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:15.240
Facebook uh marketplace. It's like, that

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:16.800
skill is so difficult to learn. Do you

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:18.840
feel like that is innate? Did you Did

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:19.520
you learn creative marketing and sales

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:21.880
or how did that work?

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:22.760
>> Yeah, so I I was at a mentor of a mentor

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:25.040
of mine

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:26.560
in college. I was a junior. It was a

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:28.120
couple weeks after the first like

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:29.400
startup. I was excited. I said, "Okay,

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:31.080
I'm an entrepreneur now. I need to meet

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:32.599
with all the entrepreneurs." I sit down

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:33.880
at coffee with this guy.

00:00:32.599 --> 00:00:35.360
And he's like, "Nick, do you like

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:36.480
sales?"

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:38.000
And something was off. I was like, "I

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:39.960
know I should say yes." But I was honest

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:41.640
with him. I was like, "Oh, no. I I hate

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:43.560
sales. I want to be the operator, the

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:45.600
visionary. I want to I picture myself

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:47.960
like on the whiteboard, you know, just

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:48.920
making decisions." And he goes, "Okay,

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:50.320
well,

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:52.840
this might be a short breakfast cuz what

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:53.840
I'm about to say might piss you off. But

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:54.920
if you don't like sales, you need to go

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:55.640
get a job."

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:58.160
>> Mhm.

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:59.080
>> And I'm like, "Whoa, what?

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:00.440
Hold on.

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:02.200
What do you mean?" And he goes,

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:04.320
"Like, if you are an entrepreneur, if

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:06.320
you want to be an entrepreneur, not only

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:07.800
are you selling your customers,

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:09.320
but you're selling your employees on

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:11.680
trusting you because you have nothing.

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:14.680
You're selling your vendors on like

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:16.320
selling to you. You're selling the real

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:18.080
estate owners on leasing a warehouse to

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:20.240
you. You're selling the

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:21.280
You're just nonstop sales all the time.

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:22.760
And then when I actually zoom out and

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:24.480
look at life,

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:26.120
man, I'm selling my freaking 5-year-old

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:29.480
to get in the car in the morning to like

00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:30.920
go to school. Life is sales. And as an

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:32.240
entrepreneur, you are selling yourself

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:34.400
all the time. Very uncomfortable

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:36.600
conversations, negotiations, trying to

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:38.720
get people to do what you need them to

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:40.480
do and get them to want to do it.

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:42.080
Um and so that

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:43.880
shook me to my core when I was, you

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:45.600
know, 21 years old.

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:46.800
Um but I took it very serious cuz the

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:48.360
rest of the conversation he told me

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:49.600
that, "Hey, nobody's naturally good at

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:51.680
sales. You got to

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:52.600
wake up and get the reps in."

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:54.080
>> Mhm.

